{
  "$comment": "N-12: THE Dock ×4 (web packages/ui dock.tsx + agent-session.tsx + the thread route, desktop crates/ui dock.rs + steer_viewer.rs + thread_screen.rs, iOS ExpUI Dock.swift + AgentSessionView.swift + ThreadScreen.swift, Android ui/components/Dock.kt + AgentSessionScreen.kt + ThreadScreen.kt; models desktop domain::dock, iOS ExpCore Dock.swift, Android domain/Dock.kt). The transcript is the ONE scroll region of a session and a thread, header to bottom edge; the Dock is the floating band painted OVER its bottom in the composer column: the DockCards, `stack.gap` apart when fanned, then THE composer (always; it never yields its slot, N-12 retires `composerYieldsToCard`). The band's measured height is the transcript's bottom padding and the jump-to-bottom offset; an edge fade sits behind it. A DockCard = the AskCard chrome (`icons`/tint per `kind`, the tinted `label`, the muted `caption`, the trailing muted `meta`) over ONE `title` line and the `open` chevron (`expandable`) or the banner's `action` word; one height per row. SEVERAL cards pile like the toasts (toast-stack.json, `stackLayout` of src/stack.ts with THIS file's `stack`, anchored at the bottom): the front card is the LAST row, the older ones peek out ABOVE it by `stack.peek` and shrink by `stack.scaleStep` per rank, `stack.visible` of them at most (`hidden` = the rest); a pointer hovering the pile or a tap on it FANS it (every card at full size `stack.gap` apart, mode `fanned`); leaving or tapping the pile again re-piles. A tap (pointer: a click) on a card OPENS it: THE bottom sheet (`sheet`): a scrim, the sheet in the composer column on wide screens (`sheet.radius` on its top corners) and edge to edge on phones (the grabber, drag to dismiss), fitting its content up to `sheet.maxHeightFraction` of the viewport; a pinned HEADER (the card's icon, label, caption, the host's meta, trailing `copy.close` as a ghost icon-xs button), ONE scrolling body, a pinned FOOTER for the primary actions; Escape, the scrim, the close glyph or a drag closes it; it slides up with motion `sheet` (slow decelerate in, standard accelerate out; reduce motion = a fade), the pile moves over `motion.pile` with the standard easing, a card enters with `motion.enter` (decelerate) and leaves over `motion.exit` (accelerate). Rows = `dockRows(sources)`, ordered `order` first (queued, tasks, suggestions, banner, then the asks oldest first by createdAt, ties by id) so the card needing the viewer is in front: `plan` (label ask-dock `planReady`, caption = the asking session's name, meta = `copy.questions` when it has any, title = the plan's first plain line, ask-dock `askDockTitle`), `question` (label ask-dock `question`), `tasks` (THE Queue of task-queue.json: label = the todo title, caption = the completed title, title = the first todo item, meta = its description; opens the full Trace), `queued` (label `copy.queued`, title = the oldest queued message; opens the list with its remove glyphs), `suggestions` (EXP-1323's suggested-tasks card while ANY item is open: label = the header's count (`3 suggested tasks`), caption = its `started` part or null, title = the first open item's title; opens the list: an open item = its title and text, the Start button and the ⋯ menu (Do it here · Start on… · Start with… · File as issue · Dismiss), a started item = the child's session card, here/filed = their one line; the footer = Start all while more than one item is open; a row with no open item stays in the Conversation), `banner` (a status strip of the session view: S-3 no paused strip ×4 (an offline host is invisible); connection lost, the usage wall, compacting, the rate-limit window, starting; the host's `icon`, `label`, `text` and tone `muted`|`warning`; `action` = its one button word; never expandable). ONE GRAY ×4 (owner 2026-10-22): every card on the band and in the transcript, the composer and the sheet wear the same opaque card fill (the design tokens' `card` composite, web `bg-glass-card-opaque`) under the card hairline; nothing translucent, no second tone. `dock({rows, expanded, openId})` = the view: `mode` none|single|pile|fanned, `rows` top to bottom, `frontId`, `openId` (null unless that row exists and is expandable), `hidden`. AUTO-OPEN: `dockAutoOpen({previous, rows})` = the id of the front-most plan or question NOT in `previous` (the ids seen so far), else null; a host opens that sheet when the view is IN FRONT (visible, the session or thread open) and leaves a card that arrived while away collapsed. The host SEEDS `previous` with every card it shows until its data has loaded (the session view: the relay is live, its history replayed; the thread: its rows arrived) and for `autoOpenGraceMs` after that, so what already waited when the view opened never opens itself; only a card arriving after that does. The relay's own asks (claude's AskUserQuestion) are `question` sources too. Answered cards stay in the transcript, closed. Model = pure `dockRows`, `dock`, `dockAutoOpen` (src/dock.ts); mirrors compare the WHOLE expected object. S-3 STORIES (owner 2026-10-28): a waiting plan or question is a STORY now (stories.json), not a DockCard. Hosts pass no `plan`/`question` source any more, the relay's own engine ask (AskUserQuestion / ExitPlanMode) included: that ask stays inline at its place in the feed (FEED-140), answerable with its hotkeys, and never becomes a story. The Dock keeps tasks, queued, suggestions and banner. Those kinds stay in the model and in these cases for old data, and `dockAutoOpen` has nothing to open. The card itself still draws INLINE in the transcript, answerable (ask-dock.json).",
